{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012FW7sKhvj5JEKLiLEWbSHf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key finding: **There are NO existing tooltip or popover components in this codebase.** There's no Popper.js dependency, no tooltip component, no popover component. The Booking.tsx has a simple `(info)` link that goes to an external URL, not a tooltip.\n\nThis means I need to **create** tooltip/popover components using the Popover API and CSS Anchor Positioning. But wait - the story says \"All tooltip and informational popover components use the popover HTML attribute\" - implying there should be existing ones to migrate. There aren't any.\n\nThe story says \"Migrating hostel site tooltips and info-popovers to these native APIs reduces JS bundle size\" - but there are none to migrate.\n \nSo my approach is to build minimal Tooltip and InfoPopover components using the Popover API with CSS Anchor Positioning, apply them to a few existing elements like the info link in Booking.tsx, and keep the total diff well under 500 lines by avoiding package changes and focusing only on the component code and styling.\n\nLet me check what dependencies are already available in package.json.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8237,"cache_read_input_tokens":35359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8237},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6a2d14e-7283-489b-bbc5-9e98631480bf","uuid":"d9462777-49da-4a89-ac4d-23da60471a34"}
