{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01D63qfkbm9JWRKbBhztB76K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the problem. The previous attempt changed the search button to a `<span role=\"button\">` inside `InfoPopover`. The InfoPopover wraps this in a `<button>` with `popovertarget`. So clicking the InfoPopover trigger button shows the popover \"Search (Ctrl+K)\" but doesn't open search. The inner `<span role=\"button\">` handles the search onClick, but it's inside the InfoPopover trigger button — the click might get intercepted by the outer button.\n\nThis is actually bad UX: clicking the search icon would show a popover saying \"Search (Ctrl+K)\" instead of opening the search dialog. \n\nThat's definitely a regression. I should take a different approach — the `title` attribute was just supplementary info about the keyboard shortcut, not something that needs to become a popover. I'll keep the InfoPopover and CSS changes, but revert the Header back to a normal button and just remove the `title` since the `aria-label` already provides the accessible name.\n\nFor the overall fix, I'm keeping the InfoPopover component and the globals.css styles, fixing the Header to remove that wrapper, keeping the HeroTrustBadges changes since they use InfoPopover correctly, removing the Tooltip component I created since it's redundant, and cleaning up those `@ts-expect-error` comments in InfoPopover since React 19 supports them. I should also check what got added to package.json in the previous attempt and make sure I'm not including that.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":74441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,